C("nerves","Self","Being nervous means I'm not ready.",
 "Your heart races before a call and you read that as a warning sign.",
 ["Nerves before something that matters are normal — they show you care.","Brooks (2014) found that people who told themselves 'I am excited' before a performance (like a speech or singing) did better than those who tried to calm down.",
  "Your body's arousal is the same in nervousness and excitement; the label you give it changes how you use it."],
 "Nerves are energy. I say 'jag är taggad' and use it.",
 ["Notice the nerves.","Say out loud: 'Jag är taggad.'","Take 3 slow breaths.","Look at your first question.","Start."],
 dict(type="scale",a="Heart racing = danger",b="Heart racing = energy for something that matters"),
 "Before your next call or email, say 'jag är taggad' out loud once.",
 src=("brooks",))
